@quiet_gecko75:

Underrated? Tiny, throw-away test accounts in ephemeral CI runs.
Spin up a new mock SaaS user for every build job, inject it via OIDC, and tear it down at the end of the stage. No long-lived keys, no accidental forks leaking them, and you still prove the exact same auth & billing workflows work. Add a 30-second expiry to every token and you’ve just auto-tested both security and edge cases for two cents.

